It does NOT cover the parts of this repository that come from, or are derived
from, the upstream project DeepSeek Whale-chan
(https://github.com/Neko3000/deepseek-whalechan). Those parts do NOT all have the
same status, and the difference matters:

  - src/domain/prompt/character.ts — a deterministic compiler written against the
    upstream character specification. Its identity and proportion wording is
    derived from upstream's specification documents, which upstream licenses
    under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. It is NOT a port of upstream code: upstream ships no
    character-side prompt compiler.
  - vendor/whalechan-image-character/references/reference-catalog.json — upstream
    catalogue metadata, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
  - vendor/whalechan-image-character/assets/reference-images/** — the 15
    reference webp images. These are OUTSIDE the upstream project's MIT and CC
    grants. Upstream's own notices say so, and add that redistribution and
    transmission to an image-generation service need the rights holders'
    permission. They are redistributed here non-commercially with attribution
    retained, on the strength of the upstream author's support for this
    integration, and they will be removed on request. Read
    THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md section 1 before reusing them for anything.

The three canonical constants quoted in src/domain/compose.ts come from upstream
code, which upstream licenses under MIT, so that file stays under MIT.

